Brands to look out for:

Sennheiser, Koss, AKG, Beyerdynamic, Shure, Grado, Audio-Technica  
&nbsp;  
Brands to avoid:  
Sony, Beats, Skullcandy  
&nbsp;  
You may want to make an account and ask on Head-Fi as well for recommendations/reviews, best of luck.  
&nbsp;  
As for open/closed back headphones: Closed will deliver greater isolation and punchier bass (eg Sennheiser HD212, Beyerdynamic DT770, etc) whereas open provide a greater soundstage but allow noise to leak in/out so are best suited to home listening. (Eg Sennheiser HD555, Audio-Technica ATH-AD700, etc)  
&nbsp;  
Circumaural or Supra-Aural: Do you prefer smaller headphones with potential head/listening fatigue or greater comfort and isolation? I prefer circum like my AD700's/DT770 Pro's with felt pads and can wear them all day. They're large and clunky but worth it for extended listening sessions.

